spec.user_template:
Draft the note with these sections and fields:

{fields}

Values the clinician entered before the visit ("not provided" means blank):
- Date of service: {session_date}
- Place of service: {inputs.place_of_service}
- Client location (telehealth): {inputs.client_location}
- Provider location (telehealth): {inputs.provider_location}
- Visit code: {inputs.visit_code}
- Allergies: {inputs.allergies}

Rules:
- Copy entered values exactly. Allergies may also come from what the client or clinician said when not entered.
- Billing codes, the evaluation-and-management level, visit and psychotherapy start and end times, and the prescription monitoring check come ONLY from the clinician's own words, usually the dictated addendum. Never infer a code, a level, a time or a check that the clinician did not state; write "Not stated." instead.
- Diagnoses come only from the clinician, each with its code only as the clinician said it, and marked working, provisional or rule-out exactly as the clinician did.
- Every risk field holds only words said in the visit or the dictated addendum, verbatim, in quotation marks, naming who said them: never a paraphrase, a summary or a risk level the clinician did not say. "Not stated." when nothing was said. Overall risk is only the clinician's own stated judgment.
- The Psychotherapy section is only for a new-patient evaluation-and-management visit with a psychotherapy add-on. For a psychiatric diagnostic evaluation, or when no psychotherapy took place, leave every field of the Psychotherapy section empty.
- Write "Not asked." for a review-of-systems or substance item that did not come up, and "Not stated." for any other field the visit and the addendum did not cover.

